This distribution (the ``docsubstrate`` core wheel/sdist built from the
allowlist in ``pyproject.toml``) contains generated compatibility tables for
the bounded Odoo 19 sale-order profile. Their Odoo source inputs and source
map are retained at the LGPL boundary in the separately versioned
``docsubstrate/odoo-adapter`` repository. The source files themselves, fonts,
and Odoo runtime are not bundled in the core distribution. The core runtime
dependency list remains empty (see ``pyproject.toml``).

The following external components are relevant to this project's broader
scope (the optional ReportLab rendering engine adapter and the separate,
LGPL-boundary Odoo addon in ``integrations/odoo/addons/docsubstrate_report``).
They are not bundled by this core distribution. Each is installed separately
by whoever chooses to use it, under its own upstream terms:

- Odoo Community 19.0 (LGPL-3.0) -- the required external runtime and API
  host for the separate Odoo addon. Not bundled.
- ReportLab 5.0.1 (BSD) -- the pinned PDF rendering dependency used by the
  included ``docsubstrate.renderers.reportlab_canvas`` and
  ``docsubstrate.engine_adapters.reportlab`` modules. It is not bundled in the
  core wheel; the public Odoo release assembler stages its exact verified
  wheel into the addon's managed ``lib/`` directory. Stock Odoo's ambient
  ReportLab 4.1.0 is not the certified alpha renderer.
- Pillow (MIT-CMU) -- ReportLab's own image-decoding dependency. Not
  bundled; the exact version pinned by stock Odoo 19 on Python 3.12 is
  10.2.0.
- charset-normalizer (MIT) -- a transitive dependency of this project's own
  clean-install tooling. Not bundled.
- psycopg2 (LGPL-3.0-or-later, with an OpenSSL linking exception) -- the
  Odoo addon's PostgreSQL driver, provided by the Odoo host environment.
  Not bundled.
- wkhtmltopdf / the WebKit component it embeds (component-specific GNU
  Library GPL terms in the referenced WebCore files) -- Odoo's existing
  fallback PDF renderer. Not bundled or invoked by the alpha's successful
  record-native route.

See ``SBOM.json`` for the machine-readable form of this list. Exact core
distribution membership is enforced by ``pyproject.toml``. The separate Odoo
adapter repository carries its own addon manifest and LGPL notice boundary.

